1
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:21,000
The awesomest love story ever told.

2
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:36,000
Valley Girl is a comedy, romance, music film directed by Rachel Lee Goldenberg.

3
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Set to a new wave '80s soundtrack, Julie, a girl from the
valley, meets Randy, a punk from the city.

4
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:06,000
They are from different worlds and find love.

5
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:21,000
Somehow they need to stay together in spite of her trendy, shallow friends.

6
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:36,000
Julie Richman, played by Jessica Rothe.

7
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Randy, played by Josh Whitehouse.

8
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:06,000
Stacey, played by Jessie Ennis.

9
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:21,000
Loryn, played by Ashleigh Murray.

10
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
Karen, played by Chloe Bennet.

11
00:46:45,000 --> 00:46:51,000
Mickey, played by Logan Paul.

12
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
Valley Girl is a 2020 American jukebox musical romantic comedy film directed by Rachel Lee Goldenberg, written by Amy
Talkington from a story by Wayne Crawford and Andrew Lane, and produced by Matt Smith and Steven J.

13
00:55:15,000 --> 00:55:21,000
It is a remake of the 1983 film of the same name and stars Jessica
Rothe, Josh Whitehouse, Logan Paul, and Judy Greer.

14
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
The film follows Julie Richman, a Valley girl, who falls in love
with Randy, a rebellious punk, during the early 1980s.

15
01:03:45,000 --> 01:03:51,000
Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer first announced a musical remake in February 2012, but it was halted until November
2016 when Goldenberg joined the project as director and Rothe was cast in the lead role.

16
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Casting announcements continued until May 2017 and principal
photography began that same month, taking place in Los Angeles.

17
01:12:15,000 --> 01:12:21,000
Following the completion of filming, Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer
scheduled the film for release on June 29, 2018.

18
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
However, the film was delayed following controversies
surrounding Logan Paul, who portrayed Mickey.

19
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:51,000
Valley Girl was released simultaneously through video on demand and in select
drive-in theaters on May 8, 2020, by United Artists Releasing.

20
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
It was initially set to receive a wide theatrical release on the same date, but
these plans were cancelled because of the COVID-19 pandemic.

21
01:29:15,000 --> 01:29:21,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics, with praise for the soundtrack, acting,
and tone, though many deemed it to be inferior to the original film.

22
01:33:30,000 --> 01:33:36,000
The film explores themes of high school, musical, romcom, remake, mall.

23
01:37:45,000 --> 01:37:51,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
